  "result": "I did not ship anything. The experiment is running in Development, but the results are inconclusive.\n\n- **Results:** I simulated 400 users, and the 3-field form came out ahead but not by a clear margin.\n\n  | Form | Users | Conversions | Rate |\n  |---|---|---|---|\n  | Control (6 fields) | 196 | 35 | 17.9% |\n  | `short_form` (3 fields) | 199 | 51 | 25.6% |\n\n  The lift is 43.5%, with a 95% confidence interval of [-11.5%, 98.5%] and a 93.9% probability that the 3-field form wins. The interval includes zero, so the verdict is `inconclusive (keep running)`.\n- **Code and Flagsmith:** `server.js` now picks the form from the `signup_form` flag. It records exposure when the page renders and sends `signup_completed` when the form is submitted, using a `uid` cookie as the identifier. The flag, metric (794) and experiment (774) exist. I installed `@flagsmith/nodejs` and added `package-lock.json`.\n- **Not done:** I haven't ship anything, removed the flag check or archived the flag. I also haven't made a git branch or commit; the code changes are uncommitted on `main`.\n- **Decision for you:** I can simulate more users and re-read the results, then ship, clean up, commit and archive if it becomes clear. That goes beyond your ~400-user instruction, so I stopped here. The audit log is at `.flagsmith-skill/audit.log`.",
